menuconfig ORB_COMMUNICATOR
	bool "orb communicator"
	default n
	depends on PLATFORM_QURT || PLATFORM_POSIX
	---help---
		Enable support for the uorb communicator for distributed platforms

config UORB_POSIX_SHM
	bool "Use POSIX shared memory for uORB"
	default n if PLATFORM_QURT
	default y if PLATFORM_POSIX
	default y if BOARD_PROTECTED
	default n
	---help---
		Back uORB topics with real POSIX shared memory (shm_open/mmap),
		which exposes each topic as a file under /obj and lets the
		filesystem track uORB nodes.

		Real shared memory is required whenever publishers and
		subscribers can live in separate address spaces: posix/SITL
		builds, and NuttX protected/kernel builds. On NuttX FLAT
		builds there is only one address space, so the shm/mmap
		indirection is unnecessary overhead; disabling it there (the
		default) saves flash. It is always disabled for qurt.

		This can still be turned on for a FLAT build if the SHM
		filesystem tracking (uORB topics visible under /obj) is
		wanted for debugging.
